Results map executor desks j, j2, j3, j4 and j5 to contract desk j; joe and
joel remain separate, and unknown desks stay excluded (JoeDesk ADR 0001).
Every new Stage-0 capture retains the executor desk in its internal book
field. FIFO lots, broker closing-execution counts and position-gap quantity
proofs keep these sub-desk books separate; published trades and day totals
use the contract desk. Broker position rows retain their exact instrument
quantities. Older journal fills without book fall back to desk. A previously
excluded J sub-desk key still in the executor ledger is re-captured through
the existing fill-hash correction path; journals are never rewritten. The
book field stays internal, with no Results contract or lock change.

OPS-556 records desk equity closes from the pusher's same
familyAdapter.projectDeskEquities -> calculateDeskEquities valuation. The
recorder reuses copyObservation/buildCandidate (including the live v2 decimal,
reconciliation, gateway, input-age and FX gates); it never uses the New York
baseline, a proxy, FIFO realised net or a subsequent day's valuation.
Desk policy, historyBasis, Today, the NY baseline and both wire contracts stay
unchanged. Equity money in Results v2 still has only amount/currency.

At the first tick after Vienna midnight, the preceding civil day's last exact
observation becomes its close if its age measured AGAINST MIDNIGHT is at most
four publication intervals: 120 seconds with the deployed 30-second cadence.
The live input-age limit remains 300 seconds; closeMaxAgeMs also caps any
alternative cadence at that limit. See hosts/hsb0/docker/compose-spec.nix
(JOE_PUSH_INTERVAL_SEC=30), pusher.mjs and desk-equity-closes.mjs.
The valuation timestamp decides the day: a 23:59:58 observation delivered at
00:00:02 is credited before rollover; a midnight valuation belongs to the new
day. Vienna DST produces 23/25-hour days. Missing, stale and inexact closes
remain null. A later inexact sample does not erase the last exact observation.
restart_gap means a whole intervening day before this recorder instance's
first tick; days missed while this instance was running use recorder_gap.
Broker observations under revision < 10 use contract_unsupported.

Ordered deployment (DEVOPS, after OPS-557 and JOED approval):

1. Commit the reviewed implementation, then prepare the r23 release set with
   a NEW immutable pusher/stager image tag and its committed runtime source
   tree. Follow the release-set prestaging/source-tree checks in the RUNBOOK;
   preserve the prior release for rollback and never overwrite a published tag.
2. Prestage that image on hsb0 and activate the r23 set while the pin remains
   null. Services use pull_policy = "never" and switch runs no --build: a Nix
   source change or equityCloseFirstDay alone keeps the old r22 image running
   and gives all-null closes. Verify the running tag/tree includes OPS-556.
3. Set nixcfg.joeResultsProducer.equityCloseFirstDay in
   hosts/hsb0/configuration.nix to a real, fixed Vienna YYYY-MM-DD ON OR AFTER
   the Vienna day that the new image became live, then apply the reviewed
   switch. Nix passes JOE_EQUITY_CLOSE_FIRST_DAY to the pusher. The next
   eligible midnight finalizes the first recorded day. Null records nothing.

Never derive the pin from the clock, move it earlier or tie it to a board
release. Durable state pins that day; a changed pin fails closed. Keep the
pin, state and outcomes across rollback. Fresh installs start on their actual
observation day without backfilling. Recovery: restore the original pin through
Nix if it changed. For invalid state, stop the pusher and restore ONLY the
private observation state from a verified backup. Without a valid state backup,
preserve the bad state in an owner-only archive and move aside ONLY that state
file under operator control. Retain the pin and current immutable outcomes;
replay preserves their committed closes. Restart without state starts today
and leaves unrecorded days unknown. Restore a matched backup pair ONLY when
the outcomes file itself is lost. An older outcomes backup loses later
committed closes and can turn previously published exact closes into null.
Preserve a corrupt outcomes stream for operator recovery; never truncate it
to make validation pass. Never invent historical observations.

Private state: /var/lib/joe-board-pusher/desk-equity-observations.json.
Handoff: /var/lib/joe-desk-equity-closes/outcomes.jsonl, a separate tmpfiles
directory (0700, uid/gid 1000; files 0600). Only that new directory is bound
read-only into Results; InaccessiblePaths hides the pusher state directory
and stager checkpoint. No raw ledger, account identity or credentials enter
the handoff. Each v1 side-file
record has schema, vienna_day, desk (j/joe/joel), closeAt, observedAt,
oldestInputAt, equityClose, reason and maxAgeMs. Null outcomes have null
observation clocks; exact amounts are EUR decimal strings of at most eight
fractional digits. Source clocks refer to the live valuation evidence.

Both files use temp-write, file fsync, rename and directory fsync. The stream
is logically append-only: atomic replacement preserves the committed prefix;
one immutable outcome per (vienna_day, desk). Identical replay adds no bytes;
a conflicting result is rejected and logged without amounts. Outcomes commit
before state advances, making boundary replay safe. hsb0 restic currently
covers only AdGuardHome, ncps and /etc, NOT these files. Operators must stop
the pusher and manually copy both files together to an owner-only off-host
archive (directory 0700, files 0600), and verify restore before relying on it.
Never truncate, rotate, reconstruct or hand-edit the live files. Startup
removes only this writer's stale UUID .tmp files; recorder errors log at most
once per reason per 15 minutes. Private state still fsyncs every tick. Corrupt
state prevents recording until operator recovery; it does not block household
publication.

The producer strictly validates the stream on every snapshot. Only exact
outcomes enrich existing activity rows from trackingStart onward. The v2
contract requires no additional desk rows; outcomes alone never create days
or desks, including on partial days where absent totals mean unknown, not zero.
FIFO still supplies activity totals and coverage. Open-day equity stays null.
Duplicate keys are unusable, even when identical. A missing/unreadable/malformed
stream yields all null plus
value-free desk_equity_close diagnostics and does not stop publication.
Null reasons stay in those diagnostics, never in Results fields or FIFO
partialReasons. Each closed day/desk since trackingStart without a recorded
outcome gets no_record, even if it has no activity row. Producer logs include
only newly changed diagnostics, at most 20 plus a summary with per-reason
counts for the entire new batch when truncated. Integrity reasons (stream
errors, duplicates, conflicts, invalid data and open days) come first; each
priority group is newest-day first. The complete value-free list is atomically
written to /var/lib/joe-results-producer/equity-close-diagnostics.json (0600)
after attempted ticks, including failed publication attempts. Unchanged lists
are not rewritten; write failures log at most once per 15 minutes and do not
stop Results publication. The outcomes reader caps its input at
64 MiB; exceeding it fails closed.

Offline validation (local cached nixpkgs, no NixOS build):
  bash tests/T100-joe-results-producer.sh
  node --test hosts/hsb0/docker/joe-board-pusher/*.test.mjs
The close tests run six mutation controls: age, start guard, conflict
rejection, exactness, null-map filtering and synthetic row creation.
verify-contracts checks both untouched wire closures.
